  {
   "evidence": "Basic.lean:65-70 and Polynomial.lean:65-69 use the identical `Fin.addCases` row function, differing only in the degree `d` read per row; `coefficientRow_dotProduct` (Basic.lean:148-156) already abstracts exactly that row for arbitrary `a b d`, so the entry computation can be stated there once.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/Polynomial/Subresultant/Polynomial.lean",
   "fix": "Abstract the shared row once in Basic.lean next to `coefficientRow_dotProduct` (line 148), e.g. `theorem coefficientRow_apply [Semiring R] {p q : R[X]} {m n : \u2115} (hm : p.natDegree \u2264 m) (hn : q.natDegree \u2264 n) (a b d : \u2115) (l : Fin (a + b)) : Fin.addCases (fun l : Fin a => if (l : \u2115) \u2264 d \u2227 d \u2264 l.val + n then q.coeff (d - l.val) else 0) (fun l : Fin b => if (l : \u2115) \u2264 d \u2227 d \u2264 l.val + m then p.coeff (d - l.val) else 0) l = l.addCases (fun l => (X ^ l.val * q).coeff d) (fun l => (X ^ l.val * p).coeff d)`, then make both `subresultantMatrix_apply_eq_coeff` and `subresultantCoeffMatrix_apply_eq_coeff` one-liners (`simp [subresultantMatrix, coefficientRow_apply hm hn]` / `simp [subresultantCoeffMatrix, coefficientRow_apply hm hn]`), deleting the duplicated case bash.",
   "issue": "`subresultantCoeffMatrix_apply_eq_coeff` (lines 91-116) duplicates `Polynomial.subresultantMatrix_apply_eq_coeff` (Basic.lean:94-117): same two-branch `Fin.addCases` case split, same `coeff_X_pow_mul'` rewrite, same `coeff_eq_zero_of_natDegree_lt` fallbacks, only with `i.val + j` replaced by `if i.val = 0 then k else i.val + j`. At `k = j` the new lemma restates the old one, since `subresultantCoeffMatrix p q m n j j = subresultantMatrix p q m n j` (Polynomial.lean:149).",
   "line": "91"
  }
 ],
